In the case of an ecommerce application, we can use category theory to model the different components of the system and their relationships. For example, we can define a category of products, where the objects are the different products in the catalog, and the morphisms are the relationships between them, such as "product A is a variant of product B". We can also define a category of orders, where the objects are the individual orders, and the morphisms are the relationships between them, such as "order A is a subset of order B".
